  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rSite Location Plan 01.05.2026;\rBlock Plan 10.03.2016;\rProposed Block Plan 24.03.2016;\rExisting and Proposed Front Elevations A-1 REVNO dated 29.04.2026;\rExisting and Proposed Rear Elevations A-2 REVNO dated 29.04.2026;\rExisting and Proposed Right Elevations A-3 REVNO dated 29.04.2026;\rExisting and Proposed Left Elevations A-4 REVNO dated 29.04.2026;\rExisting and Proposed Roof Plan A-5 REVNO dated 29.04.2026;\rExisting and Proposed Ground Floor Plans 001 RevB Dated 23.03.2026;\rExisting First and Second Floor Plans dated April 2026;\rProposed First and Second Floor Plans dated April 2026;\rOperational Details Dated 12.06.2026;   \rHeritage Statement Dated 24.03.2026;\rHIGHWAY SAFETY IMPACT ASSESSMENT.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes Order) 1 September 2020 (as Amended), the development shall only be used as a children's care home within Use Class C2 and for no other purpose whatsoever without express planning permission first being obtained from the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of residential amenity, car parking and highway safety.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be occupied by no more than 6 residents and 4 members of staff (excluding ad hoc visiting specialists/ therapists) at any one time.\r\rReason: To minimise the impact of the development on the occupiers of neighbouring properties and to manage the surrounding road network.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and to ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.\r"
  ],
